---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const updated = new Date(site.legalUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description={`${site.name} processes your images in your browser. We do not receive, store or see your files. Here is exactly what data is and is not collected.`}
  path="/privacy"
  lead={`Last updated: ${updated}`}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Short version:</strong> the files you open with our tools are processed on your own device and are never sent to us. We do not use accounts, advertising cookies or tracking cookies.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Your files</h2>
  <p>
    All image tools on {site.name} run inside your web browser. Files you select, drop or paste are read into your browser’s memory, processed there, and offered back to you as a download. They are not uploaded to our servers or to any third party, and we have no technical means of seeing them. Files are released from memory when you reset the tool, reload or close the page.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is enforced by a Content Security Policy on every page that only allows network connections to this website itself (and to the analytics service described below). Our website is a collection of static files and has no endpoint that could receive a file.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>We use your browser’s local storage for two conveniences. This data stays on your device and is never sent to us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>theme</code> — your light/dark mode choice, if you change it.</li>
    <li><code>recentTools</code> — the names of up to six tools you opened recently, shown on the home page.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can delete them at any time by clearing this site’s data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data (such as IP address, user agent, requested URL and time) to deliver pages and protect against abuse. These requests are for our web pages and program files only — they never contain your images. We do not add our own server-side logging. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views, referrers, countries and device types in aggregate. It does not use cookies, does not use local storage, and does not create a profile of you. It never receives the content or names of the files you process. We do not use Google Analytics or advertising trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site currently shows no advertising. If we introduce ads in the future (for example Google AdSense) to keep the tools free, we will update this policy before doing so, describe the cookies involved, and ask for consent where the law requires it. Ads will never have access to your files.
  </p>

  <h2>6. External links</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages link to other websites, such as OpenStreetMap from the EXIF Viewer. Those links are only followed if you click them; the map link shares only the coordinates shown on screen, not your photo.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Children</h2>
  <p>The site does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not collect personal data about you or your files, there is usually nothing for us to access, correct or delete. For data processed by our hosting provider, please see Cloudflare’s privacy policy. For questions, see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this page if our practices change, and change the “last updated” date above.</p>
</PageLayout>
